@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1798 = private unnamed_addr constant [602 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `pytest.raises` calls without an expected exception.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`pytest.raises` expects to receive an expected exception as its first\0Aargument. If omitted, the `pytest.raises` call will fail at runtime.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    with pytest.raises():\0A        do_something()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    with pytest.raises(SomeException):\0A        do_something()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: `pytest.raises`](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#pytest-raises)\0A", align 1
