@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1862 = private unnamed_addr constant [892 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `if` statements that can be replaced with `dict.get` calls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`dict.get()` calls can be used to replace `if` statements that assign a\0Avalue to a variable in both branches, falling back to a default value if\0Athe key is not found. When possible, using `dict.get` is more concise and\0Amore idiomatic.\0A\0AUnder [preview mode](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview), this rule will\0Aalso suggest replacing `if`-`else` _expressions_ with `dict.get` calls.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aif \22bar\22 in foo:\0A    value = foo[\22bar\22]\0Aelse:\0A    value = 0\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Avalue = foo.get(\22bar\22, 0)\0A```\0A\0AIf preview mode is enabled:\0A```python\0Avalue = foo[\22bar\22] if \22bar\22 in foo else 0\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Avalue = foo.get(\22bar\22, 0)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Mapping Types](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#mapping-types-dict)\0A", align 1
